<title>USA: U.S jobless claims may signal tighter labor market.</title>
<headline>U.S jobless claims may signal tighter labor market.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>A sharp drop in jobless claims last week offered fresh evidence of labor market tightness in the U.S., analysts said.</p>
<p>On Thursday morning the Labor Department said 323,000 people initiated claims for state unemployment benefits in the week ended January 11, down from a revised 355,000 the week before.</p>
<p>Wall Street experts had forecast 355,000 new claims would be filed.</p>
</text>
